{
  "case_id": "2024-24a884",
  "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government argues that the District Courts lacked equitable authority to impose universal relief"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plaintiffs allege that the Executive Order violates the Fourteenth Amendment's Citizenship Clause, \u00a7 1, and \u00a7 201 of the Nationality Act of 1940."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Argued May 15, 2025\u2014Decided June 27, 2025"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' counterarguments are unavailing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0009",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a federal court enters a universal injunction against the Government, it \u201cimproper[ly] intru[des]\u201d on \u201ca coordinate branch of the Government\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amici curiae (B. A. M. N.)",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Briefs of amici curiae urging the denial of the applications were fled in all cases for B. A. M. N. (The Coalition to Defend Affrmative Action et al.) by Shanta Driver;"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plaintiffs fled suit, alleging that the Executive Order violates the Fourteenth Amendment's Citizenship Clause, \u00a7 1, as well as \u00a7 201 of the Nationality Act of 1940, 54 Stat. 1138 (codifed at 8 U. S. C. \u00a7 1401)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government has now fled three nearly identical applications seeking to partially stay the universal preliminary injunctions and limit them to the parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government is likely to succeed on the merits of its argument regarding the scope of relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A universal injunction can be justifed only as an exercise of equitable authority, yet Congress has granted federal courts no such power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The answer is no: Neither the universal injunction nor any analogous form of relief was available in the High Court of Chancery in England at the time of the founding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Universal injunctions are analogous to this traditional equitable device, respondents say, so federal courts have authority under the Judiciary Act to issue them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents contend that universal injunctions\u2014or at least these universal injunctions\u2014are consistent with the principle that a court of equity may fashion a remedy that awards complete relief. See Opposition to Application in No. 24A884 ( CASA), at 22\u201325; Opposition to Application in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0003-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I join the opinion of the Court but write separately to note two related issues that are left unresolved and potentially threaten the practical signifcance of today's decision: the availability of third-party standing and class certifcation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0004-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in debates over the universal-injunction issue, those courts generally do not have the last word when they grant or deny preliminary injunctions. The courts of appeals and this Court can (and regularly do) expeditiously review district court decisions awarding or denying preliminary injunctive relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0004-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "applications for stays or injunctions with respect to major new federal statutes and executive actions. Deciding those applications is not a distraction from our job. It is a critical part of our job. With that understanding, I join the Court's opinion in full."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To be \u201csubject to the jurisdiction\u201d of the United States means simply to be bound to its authority and its laws. See 1 N. Webster, An American Dictionary of the English Language 732 (C. Goodrich & N. Porter eds. 1865) (defning jurisdiction as the \u201c[p]ower of governing or legislating,\u201d or \u201cthe power or right of exercising authority\u201d)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Long before the Fourteenth Amendment, and indeed before the founding, the common-law rule of jus soli (literally, right of the soil) governed English citizenship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the single additional exception of children of members of the Indian tribes owing direct allegiance to their several tribes,\u201d id., at 693."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents also sought a preliminary injunction barring enforcement of the Citizenship Order during the pendency of the litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0008",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All three District Courts preliminarily enjoined enforcement of the Citizenship Order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government fled motions to stay the injunctions in three separate Courts of Appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0010",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A stay, this Court has said, \u201c `is not a matter of right,' \u201d but rather \u201c `an exercise of judicial discretion.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a bedrock principle that parties who request a stay must show they will likely suffer irreparable harm absent such relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem, however, is that the Executive Branch has no right to enforce the Citizenship Order against anyone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0006-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The universal injunctions of the Citizenship Order ft frmly within that tradition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0007-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Massachusetts District Court \u201cdecided that a universal injunction was necessary to provide the States themselves with complete relief.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "treat children covered by the Citizenship Order as eligible\nfor federally funded welfare benefts when those children re-\nside in a respondent State. See ibid. (citing Application for\nPartial Stay of Injunction in No. 24A884, p. 23)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Stated simply, what it means to have a system of govern-\nment that is bounded by law is that everyone is constrained\nby the law, no exceptions. And for that to actually happen,\ncourts must have the power to order everyone (including the\nExecutive) to follow the law\u2014full stop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May a federal court in the United States of America order the\nExecutive to follow the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The power to compel the Executive to follow the law is\nparticularly vital where the relevant law is the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our rights-based legal system can only function properly if the Executive, and everyone else, is always bound by law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0010-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 103,
        "start": 103
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "has not yet sued carves out a huge exception\u2014a gash in the basic tenets of our founding charter that could turn out to be a mortal wound. What is more, to me, requiring courts themselves to provide the dagger (by giving their imprima-\ntur to the Executive Branch's intermittent lawlessness) makes a mockery of the Judiciary's solemn duty to safeguard the rule of law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0010-0001",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Consequently, the zone of lawlessness the majority has now authorized will disproportionately impact the poor, the uneducated, and the unpopular\u2014i. e., those who may not have the wherewithal to lawyer up, and will all too often fnd themselves beholden to the Executive's whims."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
